# v50 — vectorized packed INT4 pair load

## Differential audit finding
Original MixLLM uses packed/interleaved tensor layouts and tiled iterators, whereas current v45 decode loads two adjacent packed INT4 bytes with two independent byte loads for every DP4A group.

## Single hypothesis
Load the same two adjacent packed bytes as one aligned uint16_t from weights + k/2, then extract the low and high bytes. This preserves exactly the same packed values and asymmetric zero arithmetic while reducing one global memory instruction in the hot INT4 loop.

## Controlled change
Only the packed INT4 byte-load form changes. INT8, FP16, quantization, output mapping, model and benchmark settings remain unchanged.

## Falsification criteria
Any correctness failure rejects v50. If correctness passes but speedup is not above v45, restore v45.
